#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:221
msgid "Taxonomy Design"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:223
msgid "The taxonomy is the core intellectual contribution of a survey. It should:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:225
msgid ""
"**Be meaningful**: Categories should correspond to real methodological "
"differences, not arbitrary groupings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:226
msgid "**Be exhaustive**: Every relevant paper should fit somewhere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:227
msgid ""
"**Be mutually exclusive** (ideally): Each paper belongs to one primary "
"category"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:228
msgid "**Have informative names**: \"Attention-based methods\" > \"Category 3\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:229
msgid "**Be visualized**: A figure showing the taxonomy is almost always helpful"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:231
msgid "**Example taxonomy axes for \"LLM Reasoning\" survey:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:232
msgid ""
"By technique: chain-of-thought, tree-of-thought, self-consistency, tool "
"use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:233
msgid "By training requirement: prompting-only, fine-tuned, RLHF"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/references_paper-types.md:234
msgid "By reasoning type: mathematical, commonsense, logical, causal"
msgstr ""

